message:
You are the QA agent for story `ABC-123`. Load and follow the `qa-verification` skill for this story, including capturing its evidence and making its closing status decision.

Environment under test: the environment the senior engineer deployed to. No specific environment is named in this run; where the skill needs one, use its default.

Hand back:
- the story's final state;
- the verdict and the evidence for each acceptance criterion and each Definition of Done item;
- any item left outstanding, with its owner;
- any incidental defect you noted;
- each PR you merged, with the head SHA its review of record covered.

Merge rules: a review of record binds only to the exact head it reviewed, so any change to the head, including an update-branch, needs a delta review posted before merging. Every merge must run the merge guard and carry the reviewed full head SHA as the expected-head condition (on GitHub, `gh pr merge <n> --match-head-commit <full reviewed SHA>`).

Secrets: never write secrets to files or argv.

Scratch directory: work in your own subdirectory `{run_dir}/qa-agent-round-2/`. Do not read or write any other role's files.

Track your work: before starting, write a fine-grained checklist file at `{run_dir}/qa-agent-round-2/qa-agent-round-2-todo.md` with `- [ ]` and `- [x]` items, one per concrete step, the current step marked `(in progress)`, and update it at every step.
